{"parentUuid":"0f5ce447-1223-45ae-a294-bfdb1f1b317e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEiEMQ7gDAkte1DjZRbt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mmi65vXe7q9hvNvJUC4jk4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git checkout -q -b docs/new-code-meets-standards origin/main && /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\nc=pathlib.Path(\"CONTRIBUTING.md\"); t=c.read_text().split(\"\\n\")\ni=next(k for k,l in enumerate(t) if l.startswith(\"43. \"))\nrule = (\"44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** \"\n\"Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR \"\n\"adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, \"\n\"a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, \"\n\"status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has \"\n\"a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a \"\n\"`keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. \"\n\"For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots \"\n\"(the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 \"\n\"(the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values \"\n\"crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), \"\n\"and secrets and PII follow sections E and H. \"\n\"Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue.\")\nt.insert(i+1, rule)\nc.write_text(\"\\n\".join(t))\np=pathlib.Path(\".github/pull_request_template.md\"); s=p.read_text()\nanchor=\"- [ ] **Security implications considered** (auth, input validation, secret handling, PII in logs)\\n\"\nadd=anchor+\"\"\"\n## Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44)\n\n<!-- Tick what applies; write N/A beside a group that does not. A standard the PR cannot meet is named here with its filed issue. -->\n- [ ] **UI a11y:** new controls work by keyboard; dialogs and drawers take and return focus; every control has an accessible name; async status is announced (live region); charts have a text or table alternative; theme tokens only, both themes; new routes scanned (rule 4b) and new click-to-navigate rows have a `keyboard.spec.ts` case; checked in the accessibility tree\n- [ ] **MCP:** `mcp-honesty-reviewer` run on any `backend/app/mcp/server.py` change; sibling docstrings re-read\n- [ ] **Migrations:** `migration-safety` run; single alembic head after merging `main`\n- [ ] **Dependencies:** pinned in the single source of truth; licence gate passes\n- [ ] **Driver boundary:** values from a driver/SDK tested in the shape it returns (`driver-boundary-guard`)\n- [ ] **Published docs:** no ticket or internal-doc references; counts checked against the code\n\"\"\"\nassert anchor in s; p.write_text(s.replace(anchor,add,1))\nm=pathlib.Path(\"CLAUDE.md\"); u=m.read_text()\nu=u.replace(\"Full list (42 rules across 8 categories)\",\"Full list (44 rules across 8 categories)\").replace(\"full 42-rule working agreements\",\"full 44-rule working agreements\").replace(\"Working agreements (full 42-rule list)\",\"Working agreements (full 44-rule list)\")\nm.write_text(u)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | cat; for s in scripts/check-docs-*.py; do /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python $s >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo \"FAIL $s\"; done; echo guards-done","description":"Add CONTRIBUTING rule 44, the PR-template standards section, and fix the rule count"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1361,"cache_read_input_tokens":596490,"output_tokens":1664,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":133},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1361,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1664,"cache_read_input_tokens":596490,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1361},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Mmi65vXe7q9hvNvJUC4jk4":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && git checkout -q -b docs/new-code-meets-standards origin/main && /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\nc=pathlib.Path(\"CONTRIBUTING.md\"); t=c.read_text().split(\"\\n\")\ni=next(k for k,l in enumerate(t) if l.startswith(\"43. \"))\nrule = (\"44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** \"\n\"Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR \"\n\"adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, \"\n\"a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, \"\n\"status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has \"\n\"a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a \"\n\"`keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. \"\n\"For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots \"\n\"(the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 \"\n\"(the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values \"\n\"crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), \"\n\"and secrets and PII follow sections E and H. \"\n\"Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue.\")\nt.insert(i+1, rule)\nc.write_text(\"\\n\".join(t))\np=pathlib.Path(\".github/pull_request_template.md\"); s=p.read_text()\nanchor=\"- [ ] **Security implications considered** (auth, input validation, secret handling, PII in logs)\\n\"\nadd=anchor+\"\"\"\n## Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44)\n\n<!-- Tick what applies; write N/A beside a group that does not. A standard the PR cannot meet is named here with its filed issue. -->\n- [ ] **UI a11y:** new controls work by keyboard; dialogs and drawers take and return focus; every control has an accessible name; async status is announced (live region); charts have a text or table alternative; theme tokens only, both themes; new routes scanned (rule 4b) and new click-to-navigate rows have a `keyboard.spec.ts` case; checked in the accessibility tree\n- [ ] **MCP:** `mcp-honesty-reviewer` run on any `backend/app/mcp/server.py` change; sibling docstrings re-read\n- [ ] **Migrations:** `migration-safety` run; single alembic head after merging `main`\n- [ ] **Dependencies:** pinned in the single source of truth; licence gate passes\n- [ ] **Driver boundary:** values from a driver/SDK tested in the shape it returns (`driver-boundary-guard`)\n- [ ] **Published docs:** no ticket or internal-doc references; counts checked against the code\n\"\"\"\nassert anchor in s; p.write_text(s.replace(anchor,add,1))\nm=pathlib.Path(\"CLAUDE.md\"); u=m.read_text()\nu=u.replace(\"Full list (42 rules across 8 categories)\",\"Full list (44 rules across 8 categories)\").replace(\"full 42-rule working agreements\",\"full 44-rule working agreements\").replace(\"Working agreements (full 42-rule list)\",\"Working agreements (full 44-rule list)\")\nm.write_text(u)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | cat; for s in scripts/check-docs-*.py; do /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python $s >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo \"FAIL $s\"; done; echo guards-done","description":"Add CONTRIBUTING rule 44, the PR-template standards section, and fix the rule count"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Mmi65vXe7q9hvNvJUC4jk4":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"aff7ab40-81c5-45b5-b207-5392d121e542","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEiELvM9wvRGBjpkauU8","requestRef":"e66bcc68-7475-4ea8-a665-3310384fa106","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"91c8d762-769b-4ded-92f2-efd0909c2cc7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T03:58:40.512Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"91c8d762-769b-4ded-92f2-efd0909c2cc7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"484bc160-77e2-42c2-96e8-bcdeeb96fa10","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mmi65vXe7q9hvNvJUC4jk4","type":"tool_result","content":" .github/pull_request_template.md | 10 ++++++++++\n CLAUDE.md                        |  6 +++---\n CONTRIBUTING.md                  |  1 +\n 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\nguards-done","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3c0f14da-3c3c-4847-9ec2-8fa009e0ca7b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T03:58:41.116Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":" .github/pull_request_template.md | 10 ++++++++++\n CLAUDE.md                        |  6 +++---\n CONTRIBUTING.md                  |  1 +\n 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\nguards-done","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/.github/pull_request_template.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":52,"oldLines":6,"newStart":52,"newLines":16,"lines":[" - [ ] **`docs/progress.md` — N/A** for this PR"," - [ ] **Security implications considered** (auth, input validation, secret handling, PII in logs)"," ","+## Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44)","+","+<!-- Tick what applies; write N/A beside a group that does not. A standard the PR cannot meet is named here with its filed issue. -->","+- [ ] **UI a11y:** new controls work by keyboard; dialogs and drawers take and return focus; every control has an accessible name; async status is announced (live region); charts have a text or table alternative; theme tokens only, both themes; new routes scanned (rule 4b) and new click-to-navigate rows have a `keyboard.spec.ts` case; checked in the accessibility tree","+- [ ] **MCP:** `mcp-honesty-reviewer` run on any `backend/app/mcp/server.py` change; sibling docstrings re-read","+- [ ] **Migrations:** `migration-safety` run; single alembic head after merging `main`","+- [ ] **Dependencies:** pinned in the single source of truth; licence gate passes","+- [ ] **Driver boundary:** values from a driver/SDK tested in the shape it returns (`driver-boundary-guard`)","+- [ ] **Published docs:** no ticket or internal-doc references; counts checked against the code","+"," ## Schema migration?"," "," - [ ] No schema change"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CLAUDE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":158,"oldLines":7,"newStart":158,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## 6. Working agreements (rules above feature work)"," ","-Full list (42 rules across 8 categories) lives in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Highlights:","+Full list (44 rules across 8 categories) lives in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Highlights:"," "," ### Commit & change discipline"," Per-functionality workflow, in order:"]},{"oldStart":213,"oldLines":7,"newStart":213,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## 7. Required reading before coding"," ","-1. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — full 42-rule working agreements + DoD + commit/branch conventions","+1. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — full 44-rule working agreements + DoD + commit/branch conventions"," 2. [docs/site/adr/](docs/site/adr/) — all ADRs (architecture decisions with rationale)"," 3. [context/DataQ_platform_roadmap.md](context/DataQ_platform_roadmap.md) — the 8-week, 100-task product roadmap"," 4. The current week's milestone target (see §13 below)"]},{"oldStart":287,"oldLines":7,"newStart":287,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Story ledger (curated narrative wins — internal) | [docs/stories.md](docs/stories.md) |"," | System architecture diagram | [docs/site/architecture/overview.md](docs/site/architecture/overview.md) |"," | Architecture Decision Records | [docs/site/adr/](docs/site/adr/) |","-| Working agreements (full 42-rule list) | [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) |","+| Working agreements (full 44-rule list) | [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) |"," | Live task tracker (post-v1, per-PR status) | [docs/progress.md](docs/progress.md) — completed ledgers are archived at [docs/progress-v1.md](docs/progress-v1.md), [docs/progress-v1.1.md](docs/progress-v1.1.md) and [docs/progress-v1.2.md](docs/progress-v1.2.md) |"," | **Deploy runbook + pre-/post-deploy checklists** | [deploy/README.md](deploy/README.md) — provisioning, the `workflow_dispatch` Deploy flow, and the **pre-deploy** (CI green, docs current, migration-safe) + **post-deploy smoke** (login, UI renders, every high-level flow works, infra rolled) checklists. **Run both around every deploy.** |"," | **Static read-only demo** (Pages `/demo/`, #2419) | [frontend/e2e-demo/README.md](frontend/e2e-demo/README.md) — the real SPA built with `VITE_DEMO`, answering from API responses that CI's `frontend-e2e` job records off the seeded stack on every run (never committed); `publish-demo` republishes on each push to `main`. **A new `<Route>` must be added to `e2e-demo/routes.ts`** (a Vitest check fails otherwise). |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":187,"oldLines":6,"newStart":187,"newLines":7,"lines":[" 41. **Published docs (`docs/site/`, the `docs_dir` GitHub Pages build) never cite issue IDs or PR numbers** — no `#NNNN`, no `github.com/.../issues/…` or `/pull/…` links. Those are internal project-tracking artifacts with no meaning to an external reader of the public site; state the *behavior*, not the ticket that produced it. Also don't link a published page to an un-published internal doc (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/progress*.md`, `docs/retro*.md`, `docs/ops-log.md`) — those aren't reachable from the site and the link is dead weight for a reader outside the repo. Minimize cross-links from ordinary published pages into `docs/site/adr/` too: ADRs are design-rationale records for contributors, not the audience of a feature guide — link one only when the ADR itself is the answer to what the reader is asking, not as a routine \"see also.\" **Within `docs/site/adr/`:** ADR-to-ADR references are fine (an ADR is allowed to cite another ADR it supersedes/amends/depends on — that's the decision graph, not project tracking). ADR-to-PR references should still be minimized — an ADR records *why a decision was made*, not *which PR shipped it*; a PR link ties a durable rationale to an ephemeral implementation artifact and is exactly the class rule 41 exists to keep out."," 42. **Stable external surfaces follow the API compatibility policy** (`docs/site/reference/api-compatibility.md`): the REST API, MCP tools, the suite export document and the Python client (`dataq-client` and its CLI). An additive change needs nothing; a breaking change is announced under **Breaking** in the CHANGELOG, stays deprecated for at least one minor release before removal (security fixes excepted, still announced), and any suite-document shape change (an added field included) bumps its `version` while the previous version stays importable for a minor release. A PR that changes a stable surface says which kind of change it is."," 43. **Changelog entries are fragments, assembled at release.** A PR never edits the Unreleased part of `docs/site/reference/changelog.md`; it adds `changelog.d/<issue>.<section>.md` (`<issue>-<n>` for a second entry; section one of `breaking | security | added | changed | fixed`; body = the bullet's text without the leading `- `, bold lead phrase, no ticket numbers — rule 41). The published page renders them under **Unreleased** at build time (`docs/hooks/changelog_fragments.py`). CI fails a PR that touches user-facing paths (`backend/app/`, `frontend/src/`, `packages/`, `integrations/`, `deploy/`, `docs/site/{guides,get-started,reference}/`) without a fragment unless it carries the **`no-changelog`** label; Dependabot is exempt. At release, `python scripts/changelog.py assemble --version X.Y.Z --date YYYY-MM-DD` moves the fragments into the dated section (the step is in the release checklist, `docs/site/operate/runbook-faq.md`). Grammar and examples: `changelog.d/README.md`.","+44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a `keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots (the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 (the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), and secrets and PII follow sections E and H. Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue."," "," ---"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/.github/pull_request_template.md","/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CLAUDE.md","/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aff7ab40-81c5-45b5-b207-5392d121e542","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"