shape it returns (`driver-boundary-guard`)","-- [ ] **Published docs:** no ticket or internal-doc references; counts checked against the code","-"," ## Schema migration?"," "," - [ ] No schema change"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CLAUDE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":158,"oldLines":7,"newStart":158,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## 6. Working agreements (rules above feature work)"," ","-Full list (44 rules across 8 categories) lives in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Highlights:","+Full list (42 rules across 8 categories) lives in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Highlights:"," "," ### Commit & change discipline"," Per-functionality workflow, in order:"]},{"oldStart":213,"oldLines":7,"newStart":213,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## 7. Required reading before coding"," ","-1. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — full 44-rule working agreements + DoD + commit/branch conventions","+1. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — full 42-rule working agreements + DoD + commit/branch conventions"," 2. [docs/site/adr/](docs/site/adr/) — all ADRs (architecture decisions with rationale)"," 3. [context/DataQ_platform_roadmap.md](context/DataQ_platform_roadmap.md) — the 8-week, 100-task product roadmap"," 4. The current week's milestone target (see §13 below)"]},{"oldStart":287,"oldLines":7,"newStart":287,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Story ledger (curated narrative wins — internal) | [docs/stories.md](docs/stories.md) |"," | System architecture diagram | [docs/site/architecture/overview.md](docs/site/architecture/overview.md) |"," | Architecture Decision Records | [docs/site/adr/](docs/site/adr/) |","-| Working agreements (full 44-rule list) | [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) |","+| Working agreements (full 42-rule list) | [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) |"," | Live task tracker (post-v1, per-PR status) | [docs/progress.md](docs/progress.md) — completed ledgers are archived at [docs/progress-v1.md](docs/progress-v1.md), [docs/progress-v1.1.md](docs/progress-v1.1.md) and [docs/progress-v1.2.md](docs/progress-v1.2.md) |"," | **Deploy runbook + pre-/post-deploy checklists** | [deploy/README.md](deploy/README.md) — provisioning, the `workflow_dispatch` Deploy flow, and the **pre-deploy** (CI green, docs current, migration-safe) + **post-deploy smoke** (login, UI renders, every high-level flow works, infra rolled) checklists. **Run both around every deploy.** |"," | **Static read-only demo** (Pages `/demo/`, #2419) | [frontend/e2e-demo/README.md](frontend/e2e-demo/README.md) — the real SPA built with `VITE_DEMO`, answering from API responses that CI's `frontend-e2e` job records off the seeded stack on every run (never committed); `publish-demo` republishes on each push to `main`. **A new `<Route>` must be added to `e2e-demo/routes.ts`** (a Vitest check fails otherwise). |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":187,"oldLines":7,"newStart":187,"newLines":6,"lines":[" 41. **Published docs (`docs/site/`, the `docs_dir` GitHub Pages build) never cite issue IDs or PR numbers** — no `#NNNN`, no `github.com/.../issues/…` or `/pull/…` links. Those are internal project-tracking artifacts with no meaning to an external reader of the public site; state the *behavior*, not the ticket that produced it. Also don't link a published page to an un-published internal doc (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/progress*.md`, `docs/retro*.md`, `docs/ops-log.md`) — those aren't reachable from the site and the link is dead weight for a reader outside the repo. Minimize cross-links from ordinary published pages into `docs/site/adr/` too: ADRs are design-rationale records for contributors, not the audience of a feature guide — link one only when the ADR itself is the answer to what the reader is asking, not as a routine \"see also.\" **Within `docs/site/adr/`:** ADR-to-ADR references are fine (an ADR is allowed to cite another ADR it supersedes/amends/depends on — that's the decision graph, not project tracking). ADR-to-PR references should still be minimized — an ADR records *why a decision was made*, not *which PR shipped it*; a PR link ties a durable rationale to an ephemeral implementation artifact and is exactly the class rule 41 exists to keep out."," 42. **Stable external surfaces follow the API compatibility policy** (`docs/site/reference/api-compatibility.md`): the REST API, MCP tools, the suite export document and the Python client (`dataq-client` and its CLI). An additive change needs nothing; a breaking change is announced under **Breaking** in the CHANGELOG, stays deprecated for at least one minor release before removal (security fixes excepted, still announced), and any suite-document shape change (an added field included) bumps its `version` while the previous version stays importable for a minor release. A PR that changes a stable surface says which kind of change it is."," 43. **Changelog entries are fragments, assembled at release.** A PR never edits the Unreleased part of `docs/site/reference/changelog.md`; it adds `changelog.d/<issue>.<section>.md` (`<issue>-<n>` for a second entry; section one of `breaking | security | added | changed | fixed`; body = the bullet's text without the leading `- `, bold lead phrase, no ticket numbers — rule 41). The published page renders them under **Unreleased** at build time (`docs/hooks/changelog_fragments.py`). CI fails a PR that touches user-facing paths (`backend/app/`, `frontend/src/`, `packages/`, `integrations/`, `deploy/`, `docs/site/{guides,get-started,reference}/`) without a fragment unless it carries the **`no-changelog`** label; Dependabot is exempt. At release, `python scripts/changelog.py assemble --version X.Y.Z --date YYYY-MM-DD` moves the fragments into the dated section (the step is in the release checklist, `docs/site/operate/runbook-faq.md`). Grammar and examples: `changelog.d/README.md`.","-44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a `keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots (the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 (the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), and secrets and PII follow sections E and H. Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue."," "," ---"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/.github/pull_request_template.md","/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CLAUDE.md","/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"77b3cc5b-5a99-4413-ac64-f74179d21936","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"docs/new-code-meets-standards","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5044b2f3-a1e9-42d0-b7c5-d39133bb6edc","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
