{"parentUuid":"11ea3553-9cda-4cc5-ade2-f8ebd0a5994f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEiMdHYaGFfZRZ4BMvSR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BZ7bMh5FkA6tzCyQW9mubi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=~/.claude/projects/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/memory && cat > $M/feedback_new_code_meets_existing_standards.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: feedback-new-code-meets-existing-standards\ndescription: \"user direction 2026-10-21: a11y stays a Week-7 track, but every change shipped before then must meet the standards already in force (a11y and all others); CONTRIBUTING rule 44 + PR-template checklist (#2512)\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nThe maintainer kept the accessibility audits (#1672/#1673 and friends) in v1.3 Week 7, AND required that all new code shipped meanwhile complies with the existing standards, \"including but not limited to a11y\".\n\n**Why:** an open debt item is not a licence to widen the gap; otherwise Week 7 inherits a larger audit every week.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Every agent brief and every PR I review checks CONTRIBUTING rule 44 (PR #2512): new UI must be keyboard-operable, dialogs take/return focus, accessible names everywhere, async status in a live region, charts with a text/table alternative, theme tokens in both themes, new routes scanned (rule 4b) and new click-to-navigate rows in `keyboard.spec.ts`, verified in the accessibility tree.\n- Other surfaces: `mcp-honesty-reviewer` on `mcp/server.py`, `migration-safety` + single alembic head, licence gate, rule-41 docs, `driver-boundary-guard` for driver/SDK values.\n- A standard a PR cannot meet is named in the PR with a filed issue — never silently skipped.\n- Audit the UI shipped earlier in v1.3 against the same bar, not only future PRs.\n\nRelated: [[feedback-axe-gate-blind-spots]], [[project-a11y-track-2026-09-21]], [[feedback-llm-tools-must-state-blind-spots]].\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' \"- [DataQ — new code meets existing standards (rule 44)](feedback_new_code_meets_existing_standards.md) — user 2026-10-21: a11y audits stay Week 7, but every shipped change meets current standards incl. a11y now; check rule 44 in every brief/review\" >> $M/MEMORY.md\nB=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d/scratchpad/AGENT_BRIEF.md\ncat >> $B <<'EOF'\n- **Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44, maintainer direction 2026-10-21):** a known gap is not a licence to widen it. New UI: keyboard-operable, dialogs/drawers take and return focus, accessible names on every control and icon button, async status announced through a live region, charts with a text or table alternative, theme tokens only (check both themes), new routes in `e2e/a11y.spec.ts`, new click-to-navigate rows in `e2e/keyboard.spec.ts`, verified in the accessibility tree (not the DOM). Also: `mcp-honesty-reviewer` on any `mcp/server.py` change, `migration-safety` + a single alembic head, the licence gate, rule-41 published docs, `driver-boundary-guard` for driver/SDK values. A standard you cannot meet is named in the PR with a filed issue.\n- Commit trailer: use the attribution line your runtime gives you.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Save the feedback memory and extend the shared agent brief"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1059,"cache_read_input_tokens":600531,"output_tokens":1306,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1059,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1306,"cache_read_input_tokens":600531,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1059},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BZ7bMh5FkA6tzCyQW9mubi":{"command":"M=~/.claude/projects/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/memory && cat > $M/feedback_new_code_meets_existing_standards.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: feedback-new-code-meets-existing-standards\ndescription: \"user direction 2026-10-21: a11y stays a Week-7 track, but every change shipped before then must meet the standards already in force (a11y and all others); CONTRIBUTING rule 44 + PR-template checklist (#2512)\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nThe maintainer kept the accessibility audits (#1672/#1673 and friends) in v1.3 Week 7, AND required that all new code shipped meanwhile complies with the existing standards, \"including but not limited to a11y\".\n\n**Why:** an open debt item is not a licence to widen the gap; otherwise Week 7 inherits a larger audit every week.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Every agent brief and every PR I review checks CONTRIBUTING rule 44 (PR #2512): new UI must be keyboard-operable, dialogs take/return focus, accessible names everywhere, async status in a live region, charts with a text/table alternative, theme tokens in both themes, new routes scanned (rule 4b) and new click-to-navigate rows in `keyboard.spec.ts`, verified in the accessibility tree.\n- Other surfaces: `mcp-honesty-reviewer` on `mcp/server.py`, `migration-safety` + single alembic head, licence gate, rule-41 docs, `driver-boundary-guard` for driver/SDK values.\n- A standard a PR cannot meet is named in the PR with a filed issue — never silently skipped.\n- Audit the UI shipped earlier in v1.3 against the same bar, not only future PRs.\n\nRelated: [[feedback-axe-gate-blind-spots]], [[project-a11y-track-2026-09-21]], [[feedback-llm-tools-must-state-blind-spots]].\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' \"- [DataQ — new code meets existing standards (rule 44)](feedback_new_code_meets_existing_standards.md) — user 2026-10-21: a11y audits stay Week 7, but every shipped change meets current standards incl. a11y now; check rule 44 in every brief/review\" >> $M/MEMORY.md\nB=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d/scratchpad/AGENT_BRIEF.md\ncat >> $B <<'EOF'\n- **Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44, maintainer direction 2026-10-21):** a known gap is not a licence to widen it. New UI: keyboard-operable, dialogs/drawers take and return focus, accessible names on every control and icon button, async status announced through a live region, charts with a text or table alternative, theme tokens only (check both themes), new routes in `e2e/a11y.spec.ts`, new click-to-navigate rows in `e2e/keyboard.spec.ts`, verified in the accessibility tree (not the DOM). Also: `mcp-honesty-reviewer` on any `mcp/server.py` change, `migration-safety` + a single alembic head, the licence gate, rule-41 published docs, `driver-boundary-guard` for driver/SDK values. A standard you cannot meet is named in the PR with a filed issue.\n- Commit trailer: use the attribution line your runtime gives you.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Save the feedback memory and extend the shared agent brief"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"36a0ce90-b11c-42e9-9457-7e3fa2813682","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEiMcuTzdBARBt5dD5Jo","requestRef":"5938a656-4331-4e70-80d8-2ef74f41b403","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"492addc0-f5c4-49a3-9414-cc97f28d87f6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:00:09.957Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
