{"parentUuid":"12b56580-4900-4264-80e1-dea4a181a60f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEiPEHVdHHDx3uCqh9tf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013YvMEGMYSs22eW7MqN3LmW","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Rule-44 audit of v1.3 UI","subagent_type":"general-purpose","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d/scratchpad/AGENT_BRIEF.md first and follow it exactly, especially the \"Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44)\" item. Your lane name is `std`. Work only in your own worktree; commit + push after each logical step.\n\nTask: audit every UI surface v1.3 has shipped so far against CONTRIBUTING rule 44 (PR #2512 adds the rule; read its text in that PR with `gh pr diff 2512`), and fix what fails. The maintainer's direction: the general a11y audits (#1672 keyboard/focus across the app, #1673 screen-reader semantics across the app, #2051, #2061, #2064, #2067) stay in Week 7 — do NOT do those app-wide. Your scope is ONLY code introduced in v1.3: `git log --oneline v1.2.0..origin/main -- frontend/src` (≈20 commits, 79 files). The surfaces, at least:\n- Admin → Calendar (`/admin/calendar`): list, create/edit/delete dialog, refused-delete with linked checks.\n- Check editor additions: per-period fields (date/sum column pickers, IANA timezone select, settle hours, backfill), `yearly` switch, declared-periods multi-select and its warning, enable/disable a check (single + bulk).\n- Trend view for per-period/yearly checks: expected line, bands, backfilled markers, declared/detected period shading, \"Promote to calendar\" dialog, the table view, captions.\n- Run detail: \"How this period was judged\".\n- Admin → Settings → Automatic coverage (sensitivity, `yearly` switch), per-asset override, false-positive breakdown.\n- Admin → Settings → Usage telemetry panel.\n- Promote-legacy-webhook-to-channel action.\n- GCS and BigQuery connection forms (key-file secret textarea, help text).\n- Detected PII panel on the asset page (from #2470), pii_drift check editor fields (#2478).\n- Every dialog after the #2467 fade change.\n\nFor each surface, check in a real browser (Playwright MCP or a Playwright spec) against the seeded e2e stack the specs use (see `frontend/e2e/README.md` and the a11y memory notes in the brief context: scratch stack via `scripts/docs/capture-stack.sh` or the CI-equivalent `pnpm e2e` stack; `E2E_BASE_URL` does not persist between shell calls): keyboard-only operation (Tab order, Enter/Space, Escape closes, focus moves into a dialog on open and back to the trigger on close), accessible names (read the accessibility tree via Playwright's `ariaSnapshot()` / `accessibility` APIs, not the DOM), live-region announcement for async results (save, promote, delete refusal, test connection), chart text/table alternatives, both themes (axe runs per theme already; also check token use in new CSS/inline styles), and that new routes/rows are in `e2e/a11y.spec.ts` / `e2e/keyboard.spec.ts`.\n\nDeliver:\n1. ONE PR `fix(ui): v1.3 surfaces meet CONTRIBUTING rule 44 …` (milestone \"v1.3 Week 6 — bug fixes & security\", `no-changelog` unless a user-visible behaviour changes — then a `changelog.d/<issue>.fixed.md` against an issue you file for the batch) fixing every failure that is local to v1.3 code. Add regression coverage where the repo pattern supports it: a `keyboard.spec.ts` case per new keyboard path, axe/aria assertions in the component Vitest a11y suite (`frontend/tests/a11y/components.a11y.test.tsx`) for new components, focus-return assertions. Prove each new assertion fails against the unfixed component.\n2. A failure that is NOT local to v1.3 code (it lives in a shared component or app shell and belongs to #1672/#1673) is not fixed here: add a comment to the matching Week-7 issue with the concrete finding, and say so in your report.\n3. A findings table in the PR body: surface, check, result (pass/fixed/deferred-to-#N), evidence (accessibility-tree excerpt or test name).\n\nRun the full frontend gate and the a11y specs, `/code-review <n> --comment`, fix findings, resolve threads, merge origin/main in, confirm CI green. Do not merge. Report as the brief says."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":602965,"output_tokens":1706,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1255,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1706,"cache_read_input_tokens":602965,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1255},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013YvMEGMYSs22eW7MqN3LmW":{"description":"Rule-44 audit of v1.3 UI","subagent_type":"general-purpose","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-arijit-Coding-Python-DataQ/641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d/scratchpad/AGENT_BRIEF.md first and follow it exactly, especially the \"Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44)\" item. Your lane name is `std`. Work only in your own worktree; commit + push after each logical step.\n\nTask: audit every UI surface v1.3 has shipped so far against CONTRIBUTING rule 44 (PR #2512 adds the rule; read its text in that PR with `gh pr diff 2512`), and fix what fails. The maintainer's direction: the general a11y audits (#1672 keyboard/focus across the app, #1673 screen-reader semantics across the app, #2051, #2061, #2064, #2067) stay i