{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","prNumber":2512,"prUrl":"https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2512","prRepository":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:00:40.109Z"}
{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01L7KbEkDx4V7pgb2xKhFw23","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"a0bda4fd-a29f-4ebe-b5da-0249a6d1079d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"d338ef42-a650-40c7-a017-e1dca5ad4850"}
{"parentUuid":"f8f0d3b8-d62f-40e9-8f68-8ea23b01c5c5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEiQujqTaYXJ8jVBCxyo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#2510 is merged.** It fixes the dependency cycle between the datasource modules. The seven cyclic-import alerts close on CodeQL's next scan of `main`. Together with the four false positives I dismissed earlier, that leaves no open CodeQL alerts.\n\n**The Week 2 milestone is closed.** All 21 items are done.\n\n**New code now has to meet the existing standards, a11y included.** The app-wide a11y audits stay in Week 7. Three changes cover the rest:\n- **The rule (PR #2512).** CONTRIBUTING rule 44 says a known gap is not a licence to widen it. For new UI it spells out what the automated axe scan can't see:\n  - keyboard operation\n  - dialogs that take focus on open and give it back on close\n  - accessible names\n  - live regions for async status\n  - chart alternatives\n  - theme tokens in both themes\n  - keyboard-spec cases for new clickable rows\n  - checks in the accessibility tree\n\n  It also names the existing reviewers for MCP, migrations, licences, published docs and driver values. The PR template gets a matching checklist. I also corrected CLAUDE.md, which still said the rule count was 42.\n- **Briefs and memory.** Every agent brief now includes the rule, and it's saved to memory for future sessions.\n- **An audit of what v1.3 has already shipped.** An agent is checking every v1.3 UI surface against the rule in a real browser and fixing whatever lives in v1.3 code. Anything belonging to the shared app shell goes to the Week 7 issues. The surfaces include the calendar page, the new editor fields, the trend chart, the coverage and telemetry settings, the GCS and BigQuery forms, the PII panel and the dialogs.\n\n**Dependabot #50 and #51** are still open. The fix is on `main`, but GitHub's dependency graph still lists the old `certifi` version beside the new one, which is a stale entry on GitHub's side. I'll keep checking."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2147,"cache_read_input_tokens":604220,"output_tokens":660,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2147,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":660,"cache_read_input_tokens":604220,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2147},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"009213d2-09e9-441c-9485-b203817c1f5e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEiQuDKjbNaWBrECbcWX","requestRef":"171af341-1b21-40c0-be38-a7ae83df0952","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"80e1013a-3a15-4b60-baff-d01fce87e3d9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:00:49.488Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
