{"parentUuid":"0162fa17-38a2-4b37-aea4-37f8c0b5569b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEiYTNnKk4QyQ18ybAi9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":612020,"output_tokens":2353,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":845},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2353,"cache_read_input_tokens":612020,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14626,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"174d3960-e260-4927-8611-6d231dd51655","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEiYSyV8WURjetMkCmap","requestRef":"9549167a-beab-4afd-9c9e-8061f8ea8808","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0e40a2cb-af91-43b1-a2bd-92f5ef93ecfc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:02:41.017Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
{"parentUuid":"0e40a2cb-af91-43b1-a2bd-92f5ef93ecfc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEiYTNnKk4QyQ18ybAi9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"DataQ follows six groups of standards. None of them is a formal certification. The published security overview states this outright: the product supplies technical controls, and the organisational side (DPAs, BAAs, consent) belongs to whoever deploys it.\n\n**Privacy regulation (processor-side controls only)**\n- **GDPR, CCPA/CPRA and HIPAA:**\n  - An append-only audit log covers every mutating route, plus access events.\n  - PII is redacted at the logger.\n  - Masking follows warehouse classification tags and profiler detection. A fail-closed mode masks every column not explicitly classified.\n  - Retention sweeps run on stored data.\n- **Compliance artifacts under `docs/site/security/compliance/`:**\n  - Sub-processors list\n  - DPIA input sheet\n  - Breach-notification runbook\n  - Data-subject-rights runbook\n  - DPA/BAA drafts (need counsel sign-off)\n  - Third-party notices\n- **Not done:** SOC 2, ISO 27001 and a pen test. ADR 0013 records them as an enterprise-buyer ask.\n\n**Accessibility**\n- **axe-core gate.** Serious and critical violations are scanned on every route in both themes, against a ratcheted baseline that is currently zero.\n- **Colour contrast.** Theme tokens are tested against the WCAG contrast ratios in both themes.\n- **Keyboard spec.** A real-browser test covers the skip link, focus movement and row navigation.\n- **Rule 44 (#2512, from today).** New code must meet these bars on its own.\n- **No formal WCAG conformance claim yet.** The keyboard/focus and screen-reader audits (#1672, #1673) are Week 7.\n\n**Security engineering (CONTRIBUTING sections C and H)**\n- **Scanning:** secrets with betterleaks in pre-commit and CI; static analysis with Bandit and CodeQL.\n- **Dependency CVE gate:** pip-audit and pnpm audit block merges, alongside Dependabot alerts.\n- **Third-party Actions:** pinned to a commit SHA.\n- **Weekly scan:** an OWASP top-10 spot check on new endpoints, part of the weekly security review.\n- **Credentials:** none in tracked files, not even local ones.\n- **Audit-log tamper evidence:** a webhook anchor or an object-lock anchor.\n- **Authorization:** two axes, workspace role × per-suite grant (ADR 0033).\n\n**Licensing and supply chain**\n- **Rule 40:** permissive or weak-copyleft dependencies only, so no GPL, AGPL, SSPL, BUSL or Commons-Clause. A licence gate enforces this in CI and pre-commit.\n- **Release artifacts:** THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES in both images, and an SPDX SBOM attached to every release.\n- **Test stand-ins:** nothing in the local test environment may require a commercial licence.\n- **MCP clients:** the MCP servers used while developing get a supply-chain audit every quarter.\n\n**Open interoperability standards**\n- **OIDC** for sign-in, provider-neutral.\n- **OpenTelemetry over OTLP** for traces, logs and the new usage metrics.\n- **OpenLineage** for lineage events.\n- **SPDX** for the SBOM.\n- **Vault KV v2 API** for the secret store (OpenBao).\n- **ODCS** data contracts are planned (#1977, Week 5).\n\n**Engineering process**\n- **Commits and merges:** conventional commits, trunk-based, squash-merge only, and an agent code review on every PR.\n- **Tests:** an 80% coverage gate. Black, Ruff and mypy for Python; Prettier and ESLint for the frontend.\n- **Migrations:** backward-compatible two-step migrations, plus the upgrade-path gate from the previous release.\n- **Records:** ADRs for architecture decisions, and changelog fragments with a Rollback line per release.\n- **API compatibility policy (rule 42):** applies to the stable external surfaces.\n- **Published docs (rule 41):** they cite no tickets or internal docs.\n- **MCP tools:** their docstrings must state their blind spots.\n\nIf DataQ needs to make a formal claim, the next step would be choosing a target, such as WCAG 2.1 AA conformance or SOC 2 readiness. That is a scope decision for you, not something the current cycle is building toward."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":612020,"output_tokens":2353,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":845},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2353,"cache_read_input_tokens":612020,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"174d3960-e260-4927-8611-6d231dd51655","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEiYSyV8WURjetMkCmap","requestRef":"9549167a-beab-4afd-9c9e-8061f8ea8808","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8c7b20f0-8f4a-4d57-97d4-b4e4a87a15de","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:02:47.307Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
