{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","hash":"8ea2a267d58038911caec3b605f2ac63a1fdccc3e6f2a1ac6e225cde1de27e2f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The export route defaults to JSON, and the hand-written client handles YAML separately, so it's fine. Running the client tests, then filing the bug this uncovered and opening the PR."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mrhxu6QJdsW6fmMDqGTocT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && B=/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin; (cd packages/dataq-client && $B/python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider 2>&1 | tail -1); $B/python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py backend/tests -k \"openapi or comparison_report or docs_reference\" 2>&1 | tail -1; N=$(gh issue create --title \"OpenAPI: the comparison-report download is declared as JSON, so the generated client crashes on it\" --label \"bug,priority/P3\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 6 — bug fixes & security\" --body \"\\`GET /api/v1/runs/{run_id}/results/{result_id}/comparison_report\\` returns a CSV or XLSX file, but the route declares no response, so the published OpenAPI spec says \\`200: application/json, schema {}\\`. The generated \\`dataq-client\\` therefore calls \\`response.json()\\` on a CSV body and raises on every real call.\n\nIt is also the only one of the spec's 170 operations without a typed success response, and nothing enforces that one exists.\" 2>&1 | tail -1); echo $N","description":"Run client and contract tests; file the bug","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
