{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01L7KbEkDx4V7pgb2xKhFw23","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"a0bda4fd-a29f-4ebe-b5da-0249a6d1079d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"d338ef42-a650-40c7-a017-e1dca5ad4850"}
{"parentUuid":"bfeebd5a-773e-4799-80ce-f7b845bf0ab1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Mrhxu6QJdsW6fmMDqGTocT","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1526df3a-e61e-4f39-8325-976936482752","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:10:52.424Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
{"parentUuid":"1526df3a-e61e-4f39-8325-976936482752","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEjBBcnPGV1UQF8NoiW6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cz8HFpMLNo5vHvnmhhctvb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' \"**The comparison-report download is described correctly in the API reference.** It was documented as returning JSON, so the generated Python client failed on every download; the reference now lists its CSV and XLSX media types and the client returns the file's bytes.\" > changelog.d/2514.fixed.md && /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python scripts/changelog.py lint 2>&1 | tail -1; git add -A backend/app/api/v1/runs.py backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py docs/site/reference/openapi.json packages/dataq-client changelog.d/2514.fixed.md && git commit -q -m \"fix(api): declare the comparison report's media types; every operation must have a typed success response\n\nThe report route served CSV/XLSX but declared nothing, so the spec said JSON and\nthe generated client called response.json() on a file. The route now declares\nboth media types as binary, the client config maps them to octet-stream so the\nclient returns bytes, and test_openapi_contract fails on any operation without\na summary or a typed 2xx response.\n\nFixes #2514\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"failed|error\"; git push -q -u origin fix/openapi-contract-gate 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error|rejected\"; gh pr create --title \"fix(api): declare the comparison report's media types; every operation must have a typed success response\" --body \"Makes OpenAPI completeness a gate (maintainer direction 2026-10-21: open standards are a requirement where they apply).\n\n- **Bug (#2514):** the comparison-report download served CSV/XLSX but declared no response, so the published spec said \\`application/json\\` with an empty schema and the generated \\`dataq-client\\` called \\`response.json()\\` on a file. The route now declares both media types as binary.\n- **Client generator:** openapi-python-client 0.29.1 parses \\`text/*\\` as str and skips unknown media types, so even a correct spec produced \\`BytesIO(response.text)\\`, which raises. \\`openapi-config.yaml\\` maps the two report types to \\`application/octet-stream\\` (the generator's documented \\`content_type_overrides\\`), so the client returns bytes.\n- **Gate:** \\`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\\` fails on any operation without a summary or a typed 2xx response (204 allowed). Today: 170 operations, all summarised; this route was the only untyped one. The test fails against the unfixed route (verified).\n\n\\`export_docs_reference --check\\` and the client drift check pass; \\`dataq-client\\` tests 51 passed.\n\nFixes #2514\n\n- [x] Changelog fragment (\\`changelog.d/2514.fixed.md\\`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 6 — bug fixes & security\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git checkout -q main","description":"Add the fragment, commit, and open the OpenAPI gate PR","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_read_input_tokens":637481,"output_tokens":1153,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1153,"cache_read_input_tokens":637481,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Cz8HFpMLNo5vHvnmhhctvb":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && printf '%s\\n' \"**The comparison-report download is described correctly in the API reference.** It was documented as returning JSON, so the generated Python client failed on every download; the reference now lists its CSV and XLSX media types and the client returns the file's bytes.\" > changelog.d/2514.fixed.md && /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python scripts/changelog.py lint 2>&1 | tail -1; git add -A backend/app/api/v1/runs.py backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py docs/site/reference/openapi.json packages/dataq-client changelog.d/2514.fixed.md && git commit -q -m \"fix(api): declare the comparison report's media types; every operation must have a typed success response\n\nThe report route served CSV/XLSX but declared nothing, so the spec said JSON and\nthe generated client called response.json() on a file. The route now declares\nboth media types as binary, the client config maps them to octet-stream so the\nclient returns bytes, and test_openapi_contract fails on any operation without\na summary or a typed 2xx response.\n\nFixes #2514\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"failed|error\"; git push -q -u origin fix/openapi-contract-gate 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error|rejected\"; gh pr create --title \"fix(api): declare the comparison report's media types; every operation must have a typed success response\" --body \"Makes OpenAPI completeness a gate (maintainer direction 2026-10-21: open standards are a requirement where they apply).\n\n- **Bug (#2514):** the comparison-report download served CSV/XLSX but declared no response, so the published spec said \\`application/json\\` with an empty schema and the generated \\`dataq-client\\` called \\`response.json()\\` on a file. The route now declares both media types as binary.\n- **Client generator:** openapi-python-client 0.29.1 parses \\`text/*\\` as str and skips unknown media types, so even a correct spec produced \\`BytesIO(response.text)\\`, which raises. \\`openapi-config.yaml\\` maps the two report types to \\`application/octet-stream\\` (the generator's documented \\`content_type_overrides\\`), so the client returns bytes.\n- **Gate:** \\`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\\` fails on any operation without a summary or a typed 2xx response (204 allowed). Today: 170 operations, all summarised; this route was the only untyped one. The test fails against the unfixed route (verified).\n\n\\`export_docs_reference --check\\` and the client drift check pass; \\`dataq-client\\` tests 51 passed.\n\nFixes #2514\n\n- [x] Changelog fragment (\\`changelog.d/2514.fixed.md\\`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 6 — bug fixes & security\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git checkout -q main","description":"Add the fragment, commit, and open the OpenAPI gate PR","timeout":300000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Cz8HFpMLNo5vHvnmhhctvb":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"fa946635-e4ad-41fa-9a69-0e8e5caa8cb7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEjBBCjGF3SbAjwx3h4y","requestRef":"d02c3db1-e33f-4ce2-bfec-d7792f49d342","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"92621452-b439-4472-9de5-550565236a6e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:10:52.420Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
