{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","hash":"6bdcf6efb2bb4cd54f50fccf64026eb79f9df4d91f9073eb6c64a78a8826c1f6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cz8HFpMLNo5vHvnmhhctvb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && printf '%s\\n' \"**The comparison-report download is described correctly in the API reference.** It was documented as returning JSON, so the generated Python client failed on every download; the reference now lists its CSV and XLSX media types and the client returns the file's bytes.\" > changelog.d/2514.fixed.md && /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python scripts/changelog.py lint 2>&1 | tail -1; git add -A backend/app/api/v1/runs.py backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py docs/site/reference/openapi.json packages/dataq-client changelog.d/2514.fixed.md && git commit -q -m \"fix(api): declare the comparison report's media types; every operation must have a typed success response\n\nThe report route served CSV/XLSX but declared nothing, so the spec said JSON and\nthe generated client called response.json() on a file. The route now declares\nboth media types as binary, the client config maps them to octet-stream so the\nclient returns bytes, and test_openapi_contract fails on any operation without\na summary or a typed 2xx response.\n\nFixes #2514\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"failed|error\"; git push -q -u origin fix/openapi-contract-gate 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error|rejected\"; gh pr create --title \"fix(api): declare the comparison report's media types; every operation must have a typed success response\" --body \"Makes OpenAPI completeness a gate (maintainer direction 2026-10-21: open standards are a requirement where they apply).\n\n- **Bug (#2514):** the comparison-report download served CSV/XLSX but declared no response, so the published spec said \\`application/json\\` with an empty schema and the generated \\`dataq-client\\` called \\`response.json()\\` on a file. The route now declares both media types as binary.\n- **Client generator:** openapi-python-client 0.29.1 parses \\`text/*\\` as str and skips unknown media types, so even a correct spec produced \\`BytesIO(response.text)\\`, which raises. \\`openapi-config.yaml\\` maps the two report types to \\`application/octet-stream\\` (the generator's documented \\`content_type_overrides\\`), so the client returns bytes.\n- **Gate:** \\`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py\\` fails on any operation without a summary or a typed 2xx response (204 allowed). Today: 170 operations, all summarised; this route was the only untyped one. The test fails against the unfixed route (verified).\n\n\\`export_docs_reference --check\\` and the client drift check pass; \\`dataq-client\\` tests 51 passed.\n\nFixes #2514\n\n- [x] Changelog fragment (\\`changelog.d/2514.fixed.md\\`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 6 — bug fixes & security\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git checkout -q main","description":"Add the fragment, commit, and open the OpenAPI gate PR","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
