{"parentUuid":"cce224ca-26b9-43f5-8bad-02dd49575946","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEjKdE8VPZQU7zbatx2n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four boundary checks fail when a stray import is added, and pass on the real tree. Now the rule text."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":643794,"output_tokens":1561,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":122},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1561,"cache_read_input_tokens":643794,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3e4f8338-5261-49d3-b0ff-e5acf23c059f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEjKcjNQuwq61dd81cUc","requestRef":"d8e112a3-1b19-42c7-a0f8-6b65f1cbc063","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7c4e0b5-fb08-495d-85c4-e1877cbb37c4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:12:39.625Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
{"parentUuid":"f7c4e0b5-fb08-495d-85c4-e1877cbb37c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEjKdE8VPZQU7zbatx2n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018gT77Yss8kocakXQWzyzmj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\nc=pathlib.Path(\"CONTRIBUTING.md\"); t=c.read_text().split(\"\\n\")\ni=next(k for k,l in enumerate(t) if l.startswith(\"44. \"))\nrule=(\"45. **Interfaces use the open standard that exists for them, and the check that enforces it stays green.** \"\n\"**OpenAPI:** every REST operation has a summary and a typed success response (`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py`), \"\n\"a file download declares its media types, and `docs/site/reference/openapi.json` plus the generated `dataq-client` are regenerated \"\n\"in the same PR (both drift checks run in CI). \"\n\"**OpenTelemetry:** traces, logs and metrics are emitted through the OTel SDK and exported over OTLP from `core/otel.py`; \"\n\"a vendor exporter lives only there, no proprietary APM SDK is added, attributes follow the OTel semantic conventions with \"\n\"DataQ's own under `dataq.*`, and usage events go through the closed vocabulary in `core/usage_telemetry.py` \"\n\"(`backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py` holds the import boundary). \"\n\"**OpenLineage:** lineage events are OpenLineage run events built in `backend/app/lineage/` (same test). \"\n\"**ODCS:** a data contract is read and written as an Open Data Contract Standard document (current major, v3); \"\n\"DataQ-specific fields go in its custom properties, never a parallel format. \"\n\"**OIDC** for sign-in, **SPDX** for the SBOM, the **Vault KV v2 API** for the secret store, **conventional commits** \"\n\"and the API compatibility policy (rule 42) for versioning. A new interface with no fitting standard records that in its ADR.\")\nt.insert(i+1, rule); c.write_text(\"\\n\".join(t))\np=pathlib.Path(\".github/pull_request_template.md\"); s=p.read_text()\na=\"- [ ] **Published docs:** no ticket or internal-doc references; counts checked against the code\\n\"\nb=a+\"- [ ] **Open standards (rule 45):** REST changes keep `openapi.json` and `dataq-client` regenerated with typed responses; telemetry only through the OTel seam; lineage as OpenLineage; contracts as ODCS\\n\"\nassert a in s; p.write_text(s.replace(a,b,1))\np.write_text(p.read_text().replace(\"## Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44)\",\"## Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rules 44–45)\"))\nm=pathlib.Path(\"CLAUDE.md\"); u=m.read_text()\nfor a2,b2 in [(\"Full list (44 rules across 8 categories)\",\"Full list (45 rules across 8 categories)\"),(\"full 44-rule working agreements\",\"full 45-rule working agreements\"),(\"Working agreements (full 44-rule list)\",\"Working agreements (full 45-rule list)\")]:\n    assert a2 in u; u=u.replace(a2,b2)\nm.write_text(u)\nEOF\nB=/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin; $B/black -q backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py; $B/ruff check -q backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py && $B/mypy backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py 2>&1 | tail -1; for s in scripts/check-docs-*.py; do $B/python $s >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo \"FAIL $s\"; done; git diff --stat | cat","description":"Add rule 45, the template line, the CLAUDE.md count, and lint the test","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":643794,"output_tokens":1561,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":122},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1561,"cache_read_input_tokens":643794,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018gT77Yss8kocakXQWzyzmj":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\nc=pathlib.Path(\"CONTRIBUTING.md\"); t=c.read_text().split(\"\\n\")\ni=next(k for k,l in enumerate(t) if l.startswith(\"44. \"))\nrule=(\"45. **Interfaces use the open standard that exists for them, and the check that enforces it stays green.** \"\n\"**OpenAPI:** every REST operation has a summary and a typed success response (`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py`), \"\n\"a file download declares its media types, and `docs/site/reference/openapi.json` plus the generated `dataq-client` are regenerated \"\n\"in the same PR (both drift checks run in CI). \"\n\"**OpenTelemetry:** traces, logs and metrics are emitted through the OTel SDK and exported over OTLP from `core/otel.py`; \"\n\"a vendor exporter lives only there, no proprietary APM SDK is added, attributes follow the OTel semantic conventions with \"\n\"DataQ's own under `dataq.*`, and usage events go through the closed vocabulary in `core/usage_telemetry.py` \"\n\"(`backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py` holds the import boundary). \"\n\"**OpenLineage:** lineage events are OpenLineage run events built in `backend/app/lineage/` (same test). \"\n\"**ODCS:** a data contract is read and written as an Open Data Contract Standard document (current major, v3); \"\n\"DataQ-specific fields go in its custom properties, never a parallel format. \"\n\"**OIDC** for sign-in, **SPDX** for the SBOM, the **Vault KV v2 API** for the secret store, **conventional commits** \"\n\"and the API compatibility policy (rule 42) for versioning. A new interface with no fitting standard