ule list) | [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) |"," | Live task tracker (post-v1, per-PR status) | [docs/progress.md](docs/progress.md) — completed ledgers are archived at [docs/progress-v1.md](docs/progress-v1.md), [docs/progress-v1.1.md](docs/progress-v1.1.md) and [docs/progress-v1.2.md](docs/progress-v1.2.md) |"," | **Deploy runbook + pre-/post-deploy checklists** | [deploy/README.md](deploy/README.md) — provisioning, the `workflow_dispatch` Deploy flow, and the **pre-deploy** (CI green, docs current, migration-safe) + **post-deploy smoke** (login, UI renders, every high-level flow works, infra rolled) checklists. **Run both around every deploy.** |"," | **Static read-only demo** (Pages `/demo/`, #2419) | [frontend/e2e-demo/README.md](frontend/e2e-demo/README.md) — the real SPA built with `VITE_DEMO`, answering from API responses that CI's `frontend-e2e` job records off the seeded stack on every run (never committed); `publish-demo` republishes on each push to `main`. **A new `<Route>` must be added to `e2e-demo/routes.ts`** (a Vitest check fails otherwise). |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":188,"oldLines":6,"newStart":188,"newLines":7,"lines":[" 42. **Stable external surfaces follow the API compatibility policy** (`docs/site/reference/api-compatibility.md`): the REST API, MCP tools, the suite export document and the Python client (`dataq-client` and its CLI). An additive change needs nothing; a breaking change is announced under **Breaking** in the CHANGELOG, stays deprecated for at least one minor release before removal (security fixes excepted, still announced), and any suite-document shape change (an added field included) bumps its `version` while the previous version stays importable for a minor release. A PR that changes a stable surface says which kind of change it is."," 43. **Changelog entries are fragments, assembled at release.** A PR never edits the Unreleased part of `docs/site/reference/changelog.md`; it adds `changelog.d/<issue>.<section>.md` (`<issue>-<n>` for a second entry; section one of `breaking | security | added | changed | fixed`; body = the bullet's text without the leading `- `, bold lead phrase, no ticket numbers — rule 41). The published page renders them under **Unreleased** at build time (`docs/hooks/changelog_fragments.py`). CI fails a PR that touches user-facing paths (`backend/app/`, `frontend/src/`, `packages/`, `integrations/`, `deploy/`, `docs/site/{guides,get-started,reference}/`) without a fragment unless it carries the **`no-changelog`** label; Dependabot is exempt. At release, `python scripts/changelog.py assemble --version X.Y.Z --date YYYY-MM-DD` moves the fragments into the dated section (the step is in the release checklist, `docs/site/operate/runbook-faq.md`). Grammar and examples: `changelog.d/README.md`."," 44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a `keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots (the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 (the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), and secrets and PII follow sections E and H. Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue.","+45. **Interfaces use the open standard that exists for them, and the check that enforces it stays green.** **OpenAPI:** every REST operation has a summary and a typed success response (`backend/tests/api/test_openapi_contract.py`), a file download declares its media types, and `docs/site/reference/openapi.json` plus the generated `dataq-client` are regenerated in the same PR (both drift checks run in CI). **OpenTelemetry:** traces, logs and metrics are emitted through the OTel SDK and exported over OTLP from `core/otel.py`; a vendor exporter lives only there, no proprietary APM SDK is added, attributes follow the OTel semantic conventions with DataQ's own under `dataq.*`, and usage events go through the closed vocabulary in `core/usage_telemetry.py` (`backend/tests/core/test_open_standard_seams.py` holds the import boundary). **OpenLineage:** lineage events are OpenLineage run events built in `backend/app/lineage/` (same test). **ODCS:** a data contract is read and written as an Open Data Contract Standard document (current major, v3); DataQ-specific fields go in its custom properties, never a parallel format. **OIDC** for sign-in, **SPDX** for the SBOM, the **Vault KV v2 API** for the secret store, **conventional commits** and the API compatibility policy (rule 42) for versioning. A new interface with no fitting standard records that in its ADR."," "," ---"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/.github/pull_request_template.md","/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CLAUDE.md","/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/CONTRIBUTING.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3e4f8338-5261-49d3-b0ff-e5acf23c059f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"docs/new-code-meets-standards","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a9fb9d47-4080-42c1-88e0-6678ae06bd42","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"fix/v13-ui-rule44"}
